    {
      "blockId": "tour:itinerary_text:4b5ff9b4a37f43cc",
      "field": "itinerary.text",
      "sourceTextSha256": "ff9971500113adb03b5a3482f0969871f64fe714e117a4f4388b4c0e05762356",
      "text": "After breakfast, travel to the Pacaya volcanic complex, about 67 km from Antigua. Its main crater rises to 2,552 m above sea level. Between 1961 and March 2002, 14 major eruptions and numerous smaller eruptions were recorded.\n\nThe park covers approximately 2,065 hectares. Laguna de Calderas, a lake of about 35 hectares formed in an old crater, supplies drinking water to 11 communities and around 10,000 residents.\n\nThe hike begins at approximately 1,900 m and ascends to around 2,300 m. After the descent, transfer to Lake Atitlan.\n\nOvernight at Villa Santa Catarina. Breakfast included.",
      "provenance": {
        "kind": "ai_translation",
        "runId": "chat-w1-20261105-0058-a",
        "model": "GPT-6",
        "wordAbsenceReason": "The Word Day 3 text omits park area and Laguna de Calderas water-supply facts present in current RU; these gaps were translated from RU while route, altitudes, and hotel follow approved Word."
      }
